-- title:
--   Even rigidified pairs: existence, uniqueness, base change, lifting
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $r$ and $\bar r$ are distinct primes, and $N$ is a nonzero squarefree integer divisible by neither.
--
--   **The $r$-adic base.** $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi\in\mathcal O$ is irreducible, $\mathcal O$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete, the residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements and $(r)=(\pi)$; $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Next, $Onr$ is a characteristic-zero domain and $\mathcal O$-algebra with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, such that $Onr$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete, $\pi\,Onr$ is maximal, every element of $Onr$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi\,Onr$, every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi\,Onr$, and $Fr(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod{\pi\,Onr}$: thus $Onr$ is the complete unramified extension with algebraically closed residue field, with its Frobenius. Finally $vdet:\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) is the homomorphism characterised by $vdet(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g=u\pi^{n}$ for some $u\in\mathcal O^{\times}$.
--
--   **The Shimura-curve side.** For rationals $a,b$ the hypothesis `hB` says $0<a$ or $0<b$ and that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ is a division algebra exactly at the finite places above $r$ and $\bar r$; $\Lambda$ is a maximal order in it. The scheme $\mathcal X\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with its point assignment `pt` is a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves of level $N$ for $\Lambda$ (`IsCoarseModuli`: invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with pullback, bijectivity of the point map on algebraically closed fields, and the universal property). An auxiliary integer $n\ge 3$ prime to $r$, $\bar r$ and $N$ is fixed, $M\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with `ptF` is a fine moduli space for curves with full level-$n$ structure, and a group $G$ acts on $M$ by $\rho$ with labels $\chi:G\to\Lambda$ satisfying `IsLevelTwistAction` (the action is over the base, it realises level twisting by $\chi(g)$, and $\chi$ is multiplicative, surjective and injective modulo $n$). The morphism $p:M\to\mathcal X$ lies over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, is $G$-invariant, and takes $\mathrm{ptF}$-points to $\mathrm{pt}$-points of the underlying curve. For each prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$, $\mathcal Y_\ell\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with `ptT` is a coarse moduli space for curves with extra $\ell$-level, and $d_0,d_1:\mathcal Y_\ell\to\mathcal X$ are the two degeneracy morphisms over the base, $d_0$ forgetting the extra level and $d_1$ sending a point to the target of an $\ell$-level isogeny. Morphisms $a_r,a_{\bar r}:\mathcal X\to\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ realise the Atkin–Lehner relations at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points.
--
--   **The definite side.** For rationals $a_1,b_1$ the hypothesis `hdef` says $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ and that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ is a division algebra exactly at the places above $\bar r$; $\Lambda_1$ is a maximal order, $R_1\le\Lambda_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$, $n_1$ an adelic unit in the $r$-Hecke set of $R_1$ such that $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$, $\iota_0$ an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\to M_2(K_0)$, and $v$ a place of $\mathbb Q$ above $r$. The group $\Gamma^{t}$ is the group of units of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ lying in the local unit boxes of $R_1$ at all places other than $v$. For each prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$ elements $s_\ell$ (global) and $sf_\ell$ (adelic) are given with: $sf_\ell$ equal to $s_\ell$ at each place not above $r$ and to $1$ at each place above $r$; the product of the diagonal image of $\ell$ with $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lying in the level Hecke set of $(\Lambda_1,R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1})$ at $\ell$ if $\ell\mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set of $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ otherwise; and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$. Further $\Gamma^{t}_\ell=\Gamma^{t}\cap s_\ell\Gamma^{t}s_\ell^{-1}$, and $\bar w$ is a unit of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma^{t}$.
--
--   **The special fibre.** All rational integers lie in $\Lambda$ (`hΛℤ`), and `coord` is an order coordinatisation $\Lambda\to Zp2\,r\times Zp2\,r$ (`IsOrderCoord`: additive, unital, the twisted multiplication rule, injective, $r$-adically dense, and the trace condition). Over the residue ring $Onr/(\pi)$ there are a fake elliptic curve $A_0$ of level $N$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$, and formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of dimension $2$ for $A_0$ identifying its formal group with $X_0$ through `coord` (`IsFormalModuleVia`). Families $e,e':\Gamma^{t}\to\mathrm{End}(A_0.A)$ with degrees `deg` are given, each $e\gamma$ lying over the base, subject to the hypotheses `hE1` (each pair $(e\gamma,e'\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level structure), `hE1mul` (multiplicativity up to composition with multiplication by powers of $r$), `hE1sc` (rational-integer scalars in $\Gamma^{t}$ act by that scalar, up to powers of $r$), `hE1'` (conversely, if $e\gamma$ is a scalar up to powers of $r$ then $\gamma$ is a rational scalar), `hE2` (for every injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and of $X_0.\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $e\gamma$ is induced on formal coordinates by an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser with $E_0\varepsilon=r^{k_\gamma}\,g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$), `hE3` (for every full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$ the action of $e$ is labelled by a map $\Gamma^{t}\to\Lambda$, multiplicative and sending scalars to scalars, both modulo $n$), and `hE4` (on any fake elliptic curve over an algebraically closed field pulled back from $A_0$, every level-preserving endomorphism belonging to an isogeny pair of degree a power of $r$ comes, up to powers of $r$, from some $e\gamma$). In addition an order $R_2\le R_1$ with $r$-power denominators in $R_1$ is given together with a family $\hat e:R_2\to\mathrm{End}(A_0.A)$ over the base; the hypotheses `hE5a`–`hE5e` (summarised here) require $\hat e$ to be additive for the group law, to commute with the $\Lambda$-action and preserve the level, to be unital and multiplicative, to send rational integers to the corresponding multiplications, to satisfy $\hat e(\bar x)\circ$ followed by $\hat e(x)$ equal to multiplication by $\mathrm{nrd}(x)$, to agree with $e\gamma$ on $r$-power multiples of $\gamma$ up to powers of $r$, and to admit, jointly with $e$, the matrix description of `hE2` for both $\Gamma^{t}$ and $R_2$ with one and the same $g$.
--
--   **The formal-module side.** A ring map $\iota:Zp2\,r\to Onr$, a special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ of height $4$ over $Onr/(r)$ (special for the structure map induced by $\iota$), and a moduli package $MD$ over $Onr$ which is a Zariski sheaf are given, together with a comparison $\eta$ from rigidified objects to $MD$-points; the hypothesis `hη` has three clauses: on Noetherian bases, admissible rigidified objects have equal image under $\eta$ exactly when they are isomorphic; $\eta$ is natural under base change of admissible objects; and every $MD$-point is, locally on a finite cover of the base by principal opens, the image under $\eta$ of an admissible rigidified object. The map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action and of $\Phi.\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ is injective and its image has uniformly bounded denominators in $M_2(\mathcal O)$ (`hE₀`). The family $eD$ identifies, for each Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, the $G$-points of $MD$ over $B$ with pairs consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $Onr\to B$ and a Deligne datum for $\hat\Omega$ over $B$; the hypotheses `hnatD`, `hbijD`, `hfstD`, `hGLD`, `hPiD`, `hPiexD` require $eD$ to be natural in $B$, bijective, compatible with the structure map on first components, to translate the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action on $MD$-points into the twisted action `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct`, to translate $\pi$-translation into the Frobenius twist by $1$ on the first leg with unchanged Deligne datum, and to guarantee that $\pi$-translates exist. A ring map $\kappa:Onr/(\pi)\to Onr/(r)$ compatible with the quotient maps, an integer $n_0$ and a series $\beta_0$ exhibiting an isogeny of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to the base change of $X_0$ along $\kappa$ are fixed, as is a full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$. A curve $A_{0w}$ over $Onr/(\pi)$ with morphisms $aw,aw',bw,bw'$ and an integer $kw$ is given, where $(aw,aw')$ exhibits $A_{0w}$ as the Atkin–Lehner quotient of $A_0$ at $\bar r$, $(bw,bw')$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{kw}$ preserving the level, and `hJOINTw` asserts the matrix description of `hE2` with one $g$ for all $e\gamma$ and, simultaneously, for the composite $aw$ followed by $bw$ with matrix $r^{k_w}g\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g^{-1}$.
--
--   **The comparison map $\Xi$.** For each Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent and each $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi:Onr\to B$, $\Xi$ assigns a $G$-point of $MD$ over $B$ to each rigidified curve, that is, to each pair consisting of a fake elliptic curve $E$ of level $N$ over $B$ and a rigidification: a curve $E_b$ over $B/(\pi)$ realising the reduction of $E$, a curve $A_b$ over $B/(\pi)$ realising the pullback of $A_0$ along the residue map of $\psi$, and a level-preserving isogeny pair $(\varphi,\varphi')$ of degree a power of $r$ between $E_b$ and $A_b$. The hypotheses on $\Xi$ are `hΞleg` (over a base all of whose idempotents are $0$ or $1$, the structure map of $\Xi$ is some integral Frobenius twist of $\psi$), `hΞnat` (naturality under pullback of rigidified curves), `hΞiso` (invariance under isomorphisms of curves in the sense of `IsoVia` whose rigidifications are compared by maps on the $E_b$- and $A_b$-legs commuting with $\varphi$ up to multiplication by powers of $r$), and `hΞdef` (over a connected base with $r$ nilpotent, $\Xi$ is computed by $\eta$ applied to an admissible rigidified object transported from $\theta_0$, $\kappa$ and $\beta_0$ with twist $j\le 1$, the structure map being $\psi\circ Fr^{-j}$). Finally $g_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ is fixed, `heqΓ` asserts that translating a rigidification by $e\gamma$ moves $\Xi$ by the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$ for some integer $c$, `heqW` asserts the corresponding statement for an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ with $\bar w$ in place of $\gamma$ (over bases where $\bar r$ is invertible), and `h2` asserts that $2$ is a unit in $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Notation for the conclusion.** For $\psi:Onr\to_{\mathcal O}B$ put $\psi^{\circ}=\psi\circ Fr^{-v_0}$, where $v_0$ is the integer underlying $vdet(g_0)$. A pair $(E,\varrho)$ consisting of a fake elliptic curve $E$ of level $N$ over $B$ and a rigidification $\varrho$ of $E$ relative to $A_0$ along $\psi^{\circ}$ is called *even over $(\psi,P)$*, for $P$ a Deligne datum over $B$, when the structure map of $\Xi_B(\psi^{\circ})\langle E,\varrho\rangle$ equals $\psi^{\circ}$, and when `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` holds for $g_0^{-1}$ between $eD$ of that $G$-point and the pair $(\psi,P)$; the latter says that $\psi$ is the Frobenius twist by $v_0$ of the first leg of $eD$ of that point, and that for every full lattice $M$ the line of $P$ at $M$ is the preimage, under the base-changed isomorphism for $g_0$, of the line of the Deligne datum leg of $eD$ at $g_0M$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Four assertions hold simultaneously.
--
--   (1) *Existence.* For every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent and whose idempotents are all $0$ or $1$, every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi:Onr\to B$ and every Deligne datum $P$ over $B$, there exist $E$ and a rigidification $\varrho$ of $E$ along $\psi^{\circ}$ such that $(E,\varrho)$ is even over $(\psi,P)$.
--
--   (2) *Uniqueness.* For every such $B$ (Noetherian, $\pi$ nilpotent, idempotents $0$ or $1$), every $\psi$ and $P$, and any two pairs $(E,\varrho)$ and $(E',\varrho')$ over $\psi^{\circ}$ both even over $(\psi,P)$, there are an isomorphism $i:E.A\cong E'.A$ with $i.\mathrm{hom}$ followed by $E'.f$ equal to $E.f$ such that `IsoVia E E' i hi` holds (compatibility with the group laws, with the $\Lambda$-action, and with factorisation through the level subschemes in both directions), together with a comparison of the rigidifications: there are $ib:\varrho.E_b.A\to\varrho'.E_b.A$ with $ib$ followed by $\varrho'.g_b$ equal to $\varrho.g_b$ followed by $i.\mathrm{hom}$ and $ib$ followed by $\varrho'.E_b.f$ equal to $\varrho.E_b.f$, a morphism $uA:\varrho'.A_b.A\to\varrho.A_b.A$ exhibiting $\varrho'.A_b$ as the pullback of $\varrho.A_b$ along the identity with $uA$ followed by $\varrho.g_A$ equal to $\varrho'.g_A$, and natural numbers $i_1,j_1$ with $ib$, then $\varrho'.\varphi$, then $uA$, then multiplication by $r^{i_1}$ equal to $\varrho.\varphi$ followed by multiplication by $r^{j_1}$.
--
--   (3) *Base change.* For Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ and $B'$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\varphi:B\to B'$, a map $\psi:Onr\to B$, a Deligne datum $P$ over $B$ and a pair $(E,\varrho)$ even over $(\psi,P)$, there exist a curve $E'$ over $B'$, a morphism $g:E'.A\to E.A$ exhibiting $E'$ as the pullback of $E$ along $\varphi$, and a rigidification $\varrho'$ of $E'$ along $(\varphi\circ\psi)^{\circ}$, such that $\varrho'$ is the pullback of $\varrho$ along $\varphi$ via $g$ and $(E',\varrho')$ is even over $(\varphi\circ\psi,\ \hat\Omega(\varphi)(P))$. No connectedness of $B$ is assumed here.
--
--   (4) *Lifting of rigidifications.* For Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ and $B_0$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent and an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $p:B\to B_0$ which is surjective and whose kernel squares to zero (any two elements killed by $p$ have product $0$), for every $\psi:Onr\to B$, every curve $E$ over $B$, every curve $E_0$ over $B_0$, every morphism $g:E_0.A\to E.A$ exhibiting $E_0$ as the pullback of $E$ along $p$, and every rigidification $\varrho_0$ of $E_0$ along $(p\circ\psi)^{\circ}$ whose associated $G$-point has structure map exactly $(p\circ\psi)^{\circ}$: there exist a rigidification $\varrho$ of $E$ along $\psi^{\circ}$ and a rigidification $\varrho_0'$ of $E_0$ along $(p\circ\psi)^{\circ}$ such that $\varrho_0'$ is the pullback of $\varrho$ along $p$ via $g$, the $G$-point of $(E,\varrho)$ has structure map exactly $\psi^{\circ}$, and for every Deligne datum $P_0'$ over $B_0$ the $g_0^{-1}$-twisted action relates $eD$ of the $G$-point of $(E_0,\varrho_0)$ to $((p\circ\psi),P_0')$ if and only if it relates $eD$ of the $G$-point of $(E_0,\varrho_0')$ to $((p\circ\psi),P_0')$.
--
--   This is the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison in its representable form: it states that, over Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras with $\pi$ nilpotent, the rigidified fake elliptic curves whose associated $G$-point has untwisted structure map are classified, up to a canonical isomorphism, by points of $\mathrm{Hom}(Onr,-)\times\hat\Omega$ twisted by $g_0^{-1}$, and that this classification is stable under base change and lifts along square-zero extensions. It is the input used to produce the Čerednik–Drinfeld family over the fine moduli space in the $p$-adic uniformisation of the Shimura curve at $r$.
